    "family_reading": {
        "text": "IBM Granite is a small, open weights line. Both listed versions publish open weights, and one of the two supports reasoning. Context windows sit around 131000 tokens across the family, with maximum output near 118000 tokens, so long documents fit comfortably. Inputs and outputs are text only. Pricing is low: Granite 4.0 Micro costs $0.02 per million input and $0.11 output, while Granite 4.2 8B costs $0.06 input and $0.25 output. The facts suggest the family suits text tasks that need long context at modest cost, with open weights allowing self hosting. Limits are the text only modality, the small number of versions, and the fact that only one version supports reasoning, so reasoning work depends on that tier. Output length is generous but not unlimited.",
